&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is a product-led growth company with an unusually large organic top-of-funnel, where tens of thousands of people discover and sign up for Netlify every day. That organic motion is real and meaningful, but paid acquisition is a new investment area for the marketing team, and there&#39;s a clear opportunity to build that capability from the ground up.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Manager, Demand Generation &amp;amp; Performance Marketing, you&#39;ll own paid acquisition end to end - strategy, channel selection, budget, and the agency relationship that supports execution. You&#39;ll report to the CMO, with a planned transition to the VP of Growth Marketing as that function scales, and work closely with Marketing Operations, Data, Lifecycle, and Campaigns to make sure paid-acquired users don&#39;t just land, but convert and stick. This is a builder role at a company where the organic foundation is already strong, and your job is to build the paid layer that extends its reach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own Netlify&#39;s paid acquisition strategy end to end, including paid search, paid social, retargeting, sponsorships, and any other channels worth testing and proving out.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the call on where paid creates incremental value for Netlify. Design the tests, prove which channels and audiences drive growth our organic funnel wouldn&#39;t have delivered anyway, and decide where to scale, where to hold, and where not to spend at all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the agency relationship(s) supporting paid/performance work by setting the brief, holding the agency accountable to targets, and deciding what to bring in-house as the function matures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own budget planning, pacing, and ROI reporting for all paid spend, and make the case for where to double down or pull back.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing Operations to get attribution and UTM tracking right before scaling spend, so every dollar is measurable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define target audiences and channel mix aligned to Netlify&#39;s ICP; partner with Product Marketing on messaging inputs for paid creative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the measurement framework for CAC, signup/pipeline contribution, and payback by channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Lifecycle and Campaigns to make sure paid-acquired users flow into the right onboarding and activation journeys, not just land and drop off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As the program proves out, build the roadmap and case for a fully staffed paid/performance team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in demand generation or performance marketing, with direct ownership of a paid acquisition budget in a B2B SaaS or product-led growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience running paid search, paid social, and retargeting programs yourself - not just briefing agencies or reviewing their reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of standing up or significantly scaling a paid acquisition program at an early stage, where you had to build the infrastructure and not just optimize what was already there&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing an external agency or partner relationship, including setting performance expectations and holding partners accountable to them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of attribution and marketing measurement, and a history of partnering with Marketing Ops or Data teams to get tracking right before spend scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience marketing to developers or technical audiences, or with a PLG motion where paid acquisition runs alongside a large organic and self-serve funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Is a Great Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by building and scaling a new paid program, not just optimizing one that&#39;s already mature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think like an owner of budget and outcomes, not just a briefs-and-reports manager of an agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable moving between strategy (channel mix, targeting, budget allocation) and getting into the details yourself when it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about attribution being right before spend scales, not as an afterthought.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to build in close partnership with Lifecycle, Campaigns, and Marketing Ops rather than run paid as a separate lane that hands off a spreadsheet at the end of the quarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applying&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? &lt;strong&gt;Please apply anyway!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When applying please include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A resume or short listing of your job history &amp;amp; skills (link to a LinkedIn profile would be fine). We appreciate a cover letter explaining why you would enjoy working in this role at Netlify to get to know you a bit better, though this is not required and will not impact your application. Our mission is to “build a better web” and that cannot be done without a diversity of skill sets, backgrounds and thoughts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of everything we&#39;ve ever built at Netlify, we are most proud of our team. Netlify is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are devoted to building a team of people with diverse backgrounds and lifestyles. Driving equality empowers our team, enables us to innovate, and helps us maintain a more inclusive environment. We don’t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, age, race, military/veteran status, citizenship, pregnancy status, or any other differences. If we can do anything to provide a better interview, i.e. accommodate a disability, then please let us know by emailing &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accomodations@netlify.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@netlify.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is the most popular way to build, deploy, and scale modern web applications, empowering everyone from fast moving solo developers to enterprise teams. Millions of developers and organizations rely on Netlify as their platform of choice for composing web applications that are production ready, performant, and flexible. Now, as we embrace the next era of software development, we are embedding the same fluid, intuitive experience into the Agent Experience (AX), making it just as simple for intelligent agents to understand, interact with, and act on our platform as it is for developers. Whether your user is human or machine, Netlify ensures the path from idea to URL is seamless, fast, and deeply reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Series D company that has raised over $200M from investors such as Andreessen Horowitz, Kleiner Perkins, EQT, Bessemer, BOND, and Menlo Ventures. As a fully distributed company, we aim to create a company culture where the best idea can come from anywhere and strive to be thoughtful, compassionate, and collaborative in our work. If this sounds like something you’d like to be part of, we’re excited to connect with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netlify, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that prioritizes fairness and equity, positions our employee compensation competitively in the market, recognizes and rewards performance, and takes a comprehensive approach to our rewards package. We anchor our compensation philosophy on a market-based approach, therefore salary ranges may differ depending on the labor cost in a particular location. The salary provided is in addition to robust benefits and participation in Netlify’s equity plan. Our hiring range for this role is targeted at $150,000 - $200,000&amp;nbsp; for most US-based locations. Candidates outside the US or in premium markets should consult with their Talent Acquisition partner regarding location-based ranges, as they may be higher or lower than the average US range listed. The starting pay will be determined based on multiple factors, including expertise and skills, market demands, experience, internal equity, and applicable geographic location. These compensation packages and ranges are subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify&#39;s Customer Success team is responsible for making sure customers get real, lasting value from the platform - from onboarding through renewal and beyond. The team works closely with Sales, Product, and Marketing to help customers grow their usage, see clear outcomes, and stay engaged over time. Every motion the team runs - whether it&#39;s a renewal conversation, a feature adoption push or customer escalation - is designed to build trust and relationships that compound.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists because we have a growing book of SMB accounts that need a dedicated, consistent point of contact. As our Customer Success Associate, you’ll drive broad-stroke outreach and build the workflows to manage them well. You&#39;ll carry a book of 120+ accounts with roughly $2M in ARR, and your job is to make sure those customers are engaged, getting value, and set up for renewal. This is an entry-level role with real ownership from day one, and you&#39;ll have mentorship from senior teammates as you ramp into the commercial side of the work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the day-to-day relationship for your book of accounts, serving as the primary point of contact and keeping customers informed, engaged, and successful on the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute ideas to dashboards and workflows to track your book of business - renewal timelines, health signals, engagement levels, and expansion indicators - so nothing falls through the cracks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With guidance of leadership, drive outreach to customers ahead of renewal, lead those conversations, handle objections, and negotiate terms on flat renewals and smaller expansions, looping in Sales when a meaningful expansion opportunity emerges.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and forecast your renewal book on a rolling basis, proactively surfacing risks and creating plans to address them before they become problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use product usage data and customer outcomes to demonstrate value in renewal conversations and ongoing check-ins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for feature adoption and product expansion within accounts, and flag those signals to the Sales team to build expansion pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and synthesize customer feedback and share it with Product and internal stakeholders to inform roadmap decisions and improve the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with senior CS teammates and your manager to develop your skills in account management, commercial negotiation, and customer communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience in a customer-facing role - this could be internship work, customer service, sales support, retail, or anything that required you to build rapport and solve problems for people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with data and spreadsheets, and a genuine interest in using that data to spot trends and make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of following through: when you commit to something, you close the loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication - you can explain things simply, listen well, and adapt your approach to different audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in building a career in customer success, and curiosity about the commercial side of the business - including how renewals work, how contracts are structured, and how value gets communicated to customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re based in the Denver, Colorado area and are comfortable working remotely while participating in occasional in-person meetings and engagement with Denver-based stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role is a Great Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by building relationships and want to be the person customers actually look forward to hearing from&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive when you have ownership over a defined body of work and the freedom to figure out how to make it run better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy the process of organizing complexity - tracking multiple accounts, spotting patterns, and keeping everything moving without things slipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re drawn to roles where you learn by doing, and you&#39;re comfortable asking questions and taking feedback as you develop your skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You get excited about connecting customers to features or capabilities they didn&#39;t know they needed, and seeing that translate into real adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well within a team structure and are looking for mentorship, but you also want to take real ownership rather than just support someone else&#39;s book&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applying&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? &lt;strong&gt;Please apply anyway!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When applying please include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A resume or short listing of your job history &amp;amp; skills (link to a LinkedIn profile would be fine). We appreciate a cover letter explaining why you would enjoy working in this role at Netlify to get to know you a bit better, though this is not required and will not impact your application. Our mission is to “build a better web” and that cannot be done without a diversity of skill sets, backgrounds and thoughts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of everything we&#39;ve ever built at Netlify, we are most proud of our team. Netlify is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are devoted to building a team of people with diverse backgrounds and lifestyles. Driving equality empowers our team, enables us to innovate, and helps us maintain a more inclusive environment. We don’t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, age, race, military/veteran status, citizenship, pregnancy status, or any other differences. If we can do anything to provide a better interview, i.e. accommodate a disability, then please let us know by emailing &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accomodations@netlify.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@netlify.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is the most popular way to build, deploy, and scale modern web applications, empowering everyone from fast moving solo developers to enterprise teams. Millions of developers and organizations rely on Netlify as their platform of choice for composing web applications that are production ready, performant, and flexible. Now, as we embrace the next era of software development, we are embedding the same fluid, intuitive experience into the Agent Experience (AX), making it just as simple for intelligent agents to understand, interact with, and act on our platform as it is for developers. Whether your user is human or machine, Netlify ensures the path from idea to URL is seamless, fast, and deeply reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Series D company that has raised over $200M from investors such as Andreessen Horowitz, Kleiner Perkins, EQT, Bessemer, BOND, and Menlo Ventures. As a fully distributed company, we aim to create a company culture where the best idea can come from anywhere and strive to be thoughtful, compassionate, and collaborative in our work. If this sounds like something you’d like to be part of, we’re excited to connect with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netlify, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that prioritizes fairness and equity, positions our employee compensation competitively in the market, recognizes and rewards performance, and takes a comprehensive approach to our rewards package. We anchor our compensation philosophy on a market-based approach, therefore salary ranges may differ depending on the labor cost in a particular location. Because this role is eligible to participate in Netlify’s commission plan, our hiring range for Colorado is targeted at $69,000 - $80,000 in total on-target earnings. Candidates outside the US or in premium markets should consult with their Talent Acquisition partner regarding location-based ranges, as they may be higher or lower than the average US range listed. The starting pay will be determined based on multiple factors, including expertise and skills, market demands, experience, internal equity, and applicable geographic location. These compensation packages and ranges are subject to change and may be modified in the future.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aa Senior Account Executive, you’ll be the primary connection between GitLab and our Commercial &amp;amp; Enterprise customers, working with organizations of up to 4,000 team members to help them adopt and expand the world’s most comprehensive AI-powered DevSecOps platform. You’ll own a broad book of business across a wide range of opportunity sizes, guiding small, fast-growing teams as well as more complex projects as they modernize their software delivery with GitLab. Reporting to an Area Sales Manager and partnering closely with business development, marketing, and technical teams, you’ll run the full sales process: shaping the customer’s journey, documenting buying criteria and processes, ensuring accurate pipeline based on evidence, and sharing root-cause insights on wins and losses. In your first year, you’ll focus on building trusted relationships, delivering meaningful business outcomes for customers, and being the voice of the customer internally by contributing ideas to our public issue tracker and improving our sales handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Report to an Regional Sales Director and own a broad book of Commercial &amp;amp; Enterprise business, from new prospects to growing existing accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Manage the full sales cycle for Commercial &amp;amp; Enterprise prospects, from discovery and solution alignment through negotiation and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Support GitLab for Commercial &amp;amp; Enterprise prospects by clearly articulating our DevSecOps value proposition and aligning it to customer business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Analyze wins and losses, contribute to root cause analyses, and share lessons learned with account managers, marketing, and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Document and maintain accurate buying criteria, buying processes, next steps, and owners to ensure a reliable, evidence-based pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Contribute to improving our sales handbook and processes by documenting best practices and opportunities for refinement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Provide account leadership and direction across pre- and post-sales, partnering closely with technical teams and customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Represent the voice of the customer by contributing product feedback and ideas to our public issue tracker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Proven success in software sales, ideally in a Enterprise market context, managing a varied book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Ability to guide customers through the full buying journey, including defining buying criteria, mapping buying processes, and driving clear next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Effective communication and interpersonal skills to collaborate with business development, marketing, technical teams, and sales management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Experience documenting and maintaining accurate pipeline data and account plans based on evidence rather than assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Skill in conducting and contributing to win/loss and root cause analyses, and sharing insights to improve team performance and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Proficiency in negotiation, presenting to customer stakeholders, and leading commercial discussions to close opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Interest in GitLab, open source software, and preferably familiarity with Git, software development tools, or application lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Alignment with GitLab’s values and an interest in contributing from diverse or transferable sales backgrounds, with willingness to travel in line with company policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Commercial &amp;amp; Enterprise Sales team focuses on helping growing organizations adopt and expand GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform across their software delivery lifecycle. You’ll join a distributed group of Account Executives, sales managers, and business development team members who collaborate asynchronously across regions to manage a broad book of business in the mid-market segment. We partner closely with marketing, sales development, and technical teams to run an efficient, transparent sales process, document what works in our sales handbook, and represent the voice of the customer back into GitLab. We focus on opportunities like supporting customers through toolchain consolidation, driving platform adoption, and sharing learnings from wins and losses to continuously improve how we sell and support GitLab.&lt;/p&gt;
